    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="0744" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11385: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-01T10:00:00+08:00">December 1, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. German Ambassador<anchor n="63" xml:id="d812-f1"/> left Hankow this morning
                    accompanied by the Counsellor of Embassy for Kiukiang and Kuling on customs
                    cruiser loaned by the Chinese Government. No information can be obtained
                    regarding his mission but the natural inference is that he bears to General
                    Chiang some sort of peace proposal from the Japanese.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Peiping, Shanghai. Peiping repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d812-f1" n="63" xml:id="d812-f1-content">
